@startuml samtal-architecture-overview
' What runs where, and what leaves the host. The colour of a provider is
' its `egress` class marking (samtal_server/providers/base.py), which is
' what `server.local_only` is checked against at boot.
'
' Deliberately at overview altitude: the ordering inside one turn is in
' conversation-turn.puml, and the barge-in branches in
' barge-in-decision.puml. Anything that belongs to those does not
' belong here.
'
' Needs Graphviz (`brew install plantuml` brings it). Add
' `!pragma layout smetana` to render without it, at some cost in layout.

title samtal: what runs where, and what leaves the host

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam RectangleBorderThickness 2
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 55

actor "Person\nin the room" as Human

rectangle "ESP32-S3 device\nthin: xiaozhi firmware, one config URL" as DEV #EEF3FF {
  component "**Audio front end**\nwake word (ESP-SR), echo cancellation\nin hardware (ES7210 + ES8311),\nOpus at 16 kHz up and 24 kHz down" as AUDIO
  component "**Display**\nstt text, tts sentences" as DISP
  component "**Device MCP server**\nself.* tools: volume,\nbrightness, screen" as DEVMCP
  component "**NVS**\nota_url, websocket url,\ndevice token" as NVS
}

rectangle "samtal-server (FastAPI)" as SRV #EEF8EE {
  component "**OTA / config endpoint**\nPOST /xiaozhi/ota/, the token issuer.\nStateless HMAC-SHA256 tokens,\nso no token table to lose" as OTA
  component "**WebSocket endpoint**\n/xiaozhi/v1/, Bearer gate before\nthe accept. SessionRegistry caps\nthe count and drains on shutdown" as WS
  component "**Session**\none per connection: handshake,\nconversation loop, tool loop,\nbarge-in gates" as SESS
  component "**Tool namespace**\nbuiltin | self_* | <entry>__*,\ncollision-free by construction" as TOOLS
  component "**Agent memory** and optional\n**session capture**\nfacts per agent; wav + jsonl + json" as SIDE
  component "**Provider registry**\nbuilds the providers at startup,\nenforces server.local_only" as PREG
}

rectangle "Pipeline providers, one set per agent\ncolour = the type's egress marking" as PROV #FFFBF0 {

  rectangle "Stays on the machine\negress = False" as PLOCAL #D9EAD3 {
    component "VAD\n**silero**" as VAD #D9EAD3
    component "ASR\n**faster_whisper**" as ASRL #D9EAD3
    component "TTS\n**piper**" as TTSP #D9EAD3
  }

  rectangle "The base_url decides\negress = None" as PMAYBE #FFE9C6 {
    component "LLM\n**openai_compatible**" as LLMO #FFE9C6
    component "ASR\n**openai**" as ASRC #FFE9C6
    component "TTS\n**openai**" as TTSO #FFE9C6
  }

  rectangle "Sends session data away\negress = True" as PCLOUD #F4CCCC {
    component "LLM\n**anthropic**" as LLMA #F4CCCC
    component "TTS\n**elevenlabs**" as TTSE #F4CCCC
  }
}

rectangle "Off the host" as EXT #FFF3CD {
  component "**Anthropic API**" as ANTH #FFE082
  component "**OpenAI-compatible endpoint**\na vendor, or your own Ollama\nor vLLM on localhost" as OAI #FFE082
  component "**ElevenLabs API**" as ELV #FFE082
  component "**MCP servers**\nstdio or streamable_http" as MCPS #FFE082
}

DISP -[hidden]right- DEVMCP
DEVMCP -[hidden]right- NVS

Human --> AUDIO : speaks, or\npresses the button

NVS --> OTA : boot POST, system info
OTA --> NVS : websocket url, device token,\nprotocol version, wall clock\n(never an activation section)

AUDIO --> WS : **one WebSocket**\nbinary Opus frames + JSON control
WS --> SESS
SESS --> DISP : stt text, tts sentence_start
SESS --> SIDE
SESS --> TOOLS : one flat tool list per reply
TOOLS --> DEVMCP : tools/list, tools/call\nover the same WebSocket

PREG --> PROV : built once at startup,\nshared across sessions
SESS --> PROV : PCM in, sentences of audio out

LLMA --> ANTH
TTSE --> ELV
LLMO --> OAI
ASRC --> OAI
TTSO --> OAI
TOOLS --> MCPS

note bottom of PREG
  `server.local_only` is checked at boot and never at
  runtime: a server that started cannot later be talked
  into leaking. The class marking is authoritative, and a
  type that forgot to declare one counts as egress, so the
  omission fails the boot instead of quietly sending audio
  away.
end note

note bottom of PMAYBE
  These types cannot know their own answer: a base_url may
  name a vendor or `http://localhost:11434`. Under
  local_only they demand an explicit `egress: false` on the
  provider entry, the operator asserting that the endpoint
  stays home.
end note

note bottom of DEV
  The firmware's only tie to a backend is the OTA URL in NVS.
  Endpoints, credentials, even the reply language are
  delivered by your server at runtime, so customization lives
  in Python and not in C++ you have to reflash.
end note

legend right
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#EEF3FF>    | Device: ESP32-S3, thin firmware |
|<#EEF8EE>    | samtal-server core |
|<#FFFBF0>    | Pluggable pipeline providers |
|<#FFE082>    | Off the host |
|<#D9EAD3>    | egress = False: stays on the machine |
|<#FFE9C6>    | egress = None: the base_url decides |
|<#F4CCCC>    | egress = True: sends session data away |
endlegend

@enduml
